1. DATA LICENSE - Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
   International (CC BY-NC 4.0)
================================================================

All DATA files in this repository are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
License (CC BY-NC 4.0). This means the data is free for
non-commercial use (research, teaching, evaluation, personal and
non-profit use) with attribution. Any commercial use requires a
separate commercial license from DataDrivenConstruction, see
Section 5.

What counts as "DATA":

  - All CSV files (*.csv), including the language and market
    datasets in the country folders:
      CIS-Russia-GESN-FER-TER/       (the CIS base, 30 editions)
      Asia-China-Dinge/
      Asia-Indonesia-AHSP/
      Asia-Vietnam-Dinh-Muc/
      Europe-Greece-GGDE/
      Europe-Italy-Prezzario-Toscana/
      Europe-Spain-BCCA/
      Europe-Turkey-Birim-Fiyat/
      SouthAmerica-Brazil-SINAPI/
    and the per-market catalogs under each folder's markets/.
  - All XLSX files (*.xlsx) containing cost data.
  - All Parquet files (*.parquet).
  - All Qdrant snapshot files and vector-database exports
    (*.snapshot).
  - All JSON files whose primary content is cost-item records
    (as opposed to software configuration).
  - Any data dictionaries, taxonomies, and schema definitions
    describing the above.

Full licence text:  ./LICENSE-DATA.txt
Online:             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

What DDC licenses under CC BY-NC 4.0 is the compilation: the
harmonised schema, the translations, the World Bank PPP repricing
and the cross-classification. The underlying official norms and
prices are public facts, available under their own terms directly
from each issuer. Each country folder carries a PROVENANCE.md that
names the source, its legal basis, and the attribution to
preserve. Those source attributions must be kept in addition to
the DDC attribution below.

Attribution requirement:

  Boiko, A. (2022-2026). DDC CWICR - Construction Work Items,
  Costs & Resources [Data set]. DataDrivenConstruction.
  https://github.com/datadrivenconstruction/OpenConstructionEstimate-DDC-CWICR

  If a DOI has been registered (via Zenodo or similar), cite
  the DOI instead.

See CITATION.cff for a machine-readable citation.

Note on earlier releases:

  Some of this data (the CIS base) was previously published under
  Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 (CC BY-NC 4.0). Creative Commons
  licenses are irrevocable, so copies distributed under CC BY 4.0
  before this change remain under CC BY 4.0. The current and
  future releases are licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0 as stated above.

Note on the EU sui generis database right:

  To the extent Licensor holds a sui generis database right
  under Directive 96/9/EC (as implemented in German law in
  paragraphs 87a to 87e UrhG) over the compiled database as a
  whole, CC BY-NC 4.0 - by clause 2(a)(1)(B) of the licence -
  also licenses that right to You for non-commercial use, subject
  to the same attribution condition.

