2. CODE LICENSE - Apache License, Version 2.0
================================================================

All CODE files in this repository are licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

What counts as "CODE":

  - n8n workflow JSON files and pipeline definitions under
    "0_Workflow and Pipelines CWICR/" including the
    JavaScript, Python, R, Rust, and shell adapter scripts
    in that directory.
  - AI agent instruction files under "1_AI_INSTRUCTIONS/".
  - Python scripts (*.py), shell scripts (*.sh), and any
    build / installation scripts throughout the repository.
  - Dockerfiles and docker-compose definitions.

Full licence text:  ./LICENSE-CODE.txt
Online:             https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Apache-2.0 was chosen (rather than MIT) specifically because
several of the CODE components use AI / LLM integrations and an
explicit patent-licence grant protects downstream users against
submarine-patent claims.

